    { book: "rescue", title: "RESCUE · $5 ADD", note: "One of ORIGINAL's trades turns against her, her side gets to 4x+ and price pushes into one of her lines: a $5 add on the same side, held to the bell." },
    { book: "brk", title: "BREAK ⚡ · 24H TEST", note: "Every entry any ledger takes (first one per window). Out the moment the line she entered on breaks with a strong push (1m close through by BTC $20 / gold $0.40, or two closes through). Otherwise a hard take profit." },
    { book: "hold90", title: "HOLD 90 ✦", note: "ORIGINAL's entries, hard take profit. A clear winner (past the strike by BTC $100 / gold $1.50, no line in between) rides for 90% of the max, backstopped at the take-profit line." },
    { book: "bank2", title: "BANK 2 ⛨", note: "Same entries as BANK, gentler bank from the lab: arms at +30% → +40%, gives back 10% of the peak instead of 5%, no band-tap. Being tuned this week." },
    { book: "sole5", title: "5M · SOLE", note: "Every desk setup, judged ONLY by the session bands + the 5m nav (purple, upper, lower): never in the 25% of the channel closest to the line in front. 1.38x+." },
    { book: "squeeze", title: "SQUEEZE ◫ · TWIN", note: "The live books trade for trade, except a bounce boxed in a squeeze (pocket under 0.6 of a 5m candle, or 2+ lines stacked right in front): she waits and trades whichever line a 1-minute candle closes through. Paper; side-by-side test this week." },
    { book: "brickc", title: "BRICK · CLEAN", note: "BRICK exactly, minus her rejections off a nav purple that stands alone. A purple rejection only counts when a session band (VWAP or σ) sits right on it (within 0.08σ, about $4 on BTC)." },
    { book: "brickt", title: "BRICK · TVC GOLD", note: "BRICK's gold logic read from TVC:GOLD. Since Oct 6 ~7:30 AM PT the whole desk reads gold from TVC (Love: \"CHANGE GOLD TO TVC\"), so this now fires with BRICK on gold, most often the same second. Live on Kalshi when its RUN is on." },
    { book: "brickp", title: "BRICK · PUSH", note: "BRICK, but she waits to see how price behaves at the purple (Love, Oct 6 night). A break through a purple or a 5m rejection: in at once. Any other BRICK signal with an unbroken purple just in front (within 0.5 sd): she watches it. A 1m close through it = in with the break; a tap then a 1m close back off it = in on the rejection; neither before the last 2 minutes = no trade. Every BRICK gate re-checked at entry, BRICK's exits. Paper." },
    { book: "bricks", title: "BRICK · SESSION", note: "Claude's pick from the loss lab (Oct 7): BRICK's signals off her SESSION bands only (VWAP and the sigma bands), nothing off the purples or nav bands. Session-band breaks were the best setup across 1,211 paper trades and held up in both halves. Same gates, BRICK's exits. Paper." },
    { book: "brickcr", title: "BRICK · CLEAN · RIDE", note: "BRICK · CLEAN's exact entries with no take-profit gate and no lock the win (Love, Oct 7): 90% of the max then the 1% trail, or the bell. Lab: riding past the gates and locks cost $2,064 on paper over 409 early exits (149 of them lost at the bell). Watching it live. Paper." },
    { book: "brickc75", title: "BRICK · CLEAN · 75%", note: "BRICK · CLEAN's exact entries and exits plus a hard take profit at 75% of the max (Love, Oct 7: \"can we try taking 75% of whats available?\"). Lab: -$973 on paper vs now, because the trades that run to 90%+ get capped. Watching it live. Paper." },
    { book: "brickcf", title: "BRICK · CLEAN · AFTER FEES", note: "BRICK · CLEAN exactly as the desk trades it now (buys at the ask, sells into the bid), with Kalshi's fees taken out: 7% x contracts x price x (1 - price) per fill. The yardstick for MAKER. Paper." },
    { book: "brickcm", title: "BRICK · CLEAN · MAKER", note: "BRICK · CLEAN, but she prices her own entry (Love, Oct 7: \"can she price them to get in at the best multiple she can?\"): a resting buy at the BID the moment the signal fires, which pays no fee and a better multiple. If the ask doesn't come down to it in 45 s, she buys at the ask then (fee) if it's still 1.37x+. Fees taken out, so compare with AFTER FEES. Paper." },
    { book: "brickcpt", title: "BRICK · CLEAN · PATIENT", note: "BRICK · CLEAN exactly, except she won't take an early exit (gate or lock the win) while price is moderately past the strike: gold $0.50-$1.50, BTC $25-$50. In the exit lab those were the early exits that would have paid more riding (+$1,600 over 499 exits). A few weeks on paper first (Love, Oct 7)." },
    { book: "brickcx", title: "BRICK · CLEAN · CUT 2 BANDS", note: "Love's cut-loss rule (Oct 7): BRICK · CLEAN, plus out if a 1-minute candle closes back through the line she entered on AND the next of her lines beyond it, while the bid still pays back at least half the stake. A week on paper next to the live books." },
    { book: "brickcw", title: "BRICK · CLEAN · CUT WALL", note: "Claude's cut-loss rule (Oct 7): BRICK · CLEAN, plus out if price is on the losing side of the strike and one of her unbroken lines now stands between price and the strike (her own entry rule turned into an exit), 2+ minutes in, while the bid still pays back 35%+. Paper." },
    { book: "brickcl", title: "BRICK · CLEAN · CUT LATE", note: "Claude's cut-loss rule (Oct 7): BRICK · CLEAN, plus out with 5 minutes or less left when price is on the losing side of the strike by gold $1 / BTC $50+, while the bid still pays back half the stake. Paper." },
    { book: "brickch", title: "BRICK · CLEAN · HALF AT 75%", note: "Love's scale-out (Oct 7): BRICK · CLEAN, but the first time the bid reaches 75% of the max, half is sold right there; the other half keeps every rule (take profit, gates, lock the win, the bell). Lab: helps the trades that end on a gate (+$155 gold / +$324 BTC) but costs overall (-$400 gold / -$45 BTC) by halving the full winners. Watching it live. Paper." },
    { book: "vine", title: "VINE ✨", note: "Love's hand-picked setups (Oct 8): only the 23 asset + side + setup combos from her SETUPS board, nothing else (Tap-reject at -0.5σ BTC down/up, Open -0.5σ gold up, Break-retest through +1σ gold up, Gold clock up, Tap-reject at -1.5σ gold up/down and BTC down, Fade off -1σ gold up, Tap-reject at -1σ gold up, +1.5σ BTC down, Close above +1σ BTC up, +2σ gold up, Close above +0.5σ gold up, +1σ BTC up/down, Break-retest through -1σ BTC down, +3σ and +2.5σ BTC up, Open -1σ BTC up and gold up). One trade per window, 1.38x+, NEW's exits. Silver ones wait for a silver lane. Paper." },
    { book: "anchor", title: "ANCHOR ⚓", note: "Claude's pick (Oct 8): only the two setups that won in BOTH records we have (this week's paper and the older hit book): BTC short tap-reject at +1.5σ (12/14 and 12-3) and gold short tap-reject at -1.5σ (18/24 and 19-8). Every other 'best' setup flipped between the two. Rare, on purpose. Paper." },
    { book: "rvw", title: "REVERSAL · WORST HOURS", note: "Love's idea (Oct 8): BTC only, only in the hours PRIME HOURS skips (the ones that lost money this week). Waits for price to break through one session line and tap the next, then takes the reversal back the other way at 1.38x+. $30, usual exits. Paper." },
    { book: "snapb", title: "SNAPBACK", note: "The data's answer to Love's candle idea (Oct 8): gold + silver only. When the last 15m window was already decided with 5 minutes left (95c+ either way), she takes the OTHER side at minute 1-2 (30-70c), $30, held to the bell. Look-back Sep 21 - Oct 8: right 56% gold / 58% silver, about +$1,480 together." },
    { book: "snpt", title: "SNAPBACK · TVC LINES", note: "SNAPBACK's twin on TVC's lines (Love, Oct 9: 'snapback set on the chart that respects lines best'). TVC:SILVER held 64% of line touches vs 50-54% on every other silver feed. Same trade, gold + silver, only when TVC shows price tagged a line in the decided candle's direction and closed back, and it isn't stretched 1 sigma+ past VWAP. Look-back Sep 21 - Oct 9: silver 67% (67 trades, +$565), gold 62.5% (80, +$500). Paper only." },
    { book: "b11", title: "BRICK 1:1 · REAL", note: "Love's 'what if she fired together' test, priced like Kalshi really would (Oct 9). Every BRICK trade copied the instant it books, no band waits, $22. Entry walks Kalshi's real order book up to the live limit (never past 72c); if nobody sells there it's a NO FILL. Exits sell into the real bids with the taker fee; the bell pays $1/$0 with no fee. Paper only." },
    { book: "cfol", title: "CANDLE FOLLOW", note: "Love's candle idea as she said it (Oct 8): BTC, gold and silver. When the last 15m window was already decided with 5 minutes left, she follows it into the next window at minute 1-2 (30-70c), $30, held to the bell. Look-back said it loses (42-49% right); running so we can watch it live next to SNAPBACK." },
